    86	## Decision rules
    87	- ARM 1 alone is a measurement: no ship decision follows from it. It sets the baseline for arm 2 and is cited in the dec 061 (i)
    88	  v004 cap discussion. Arm 1 is INVALID (env problem, not a quality result) iff H rows >= 5 of 33, whatever the pass count.
    89	- ENV CONTROL (pre-registered follow-up, not gating the runs): a gold+null pass of the 33 dev ids through this exact kernel
    90	  verification path (CPU kernel, no GPU quota; needs a small gold-patch mode, codex-reviewed first). Until it exists, arm 1 is
    91	  reported with the caveat "env agreement with the local gold calibration unmeasured in the kernel path". When it exists:
    92	  ids whose kernel-path gold fails or null passes are listed and a sensitivity pass rate excludes them; the primary is unchanged.
    93	- ARM 2 vs ARM 1 (paired, same 33 ids, k=1 FIXED: no second sample under this plan, whatever arm 2 shows): per-task discordant
    94	  counts on-only / off-only, exact two-sided sign test. Any later k>1 needs a new pre-registration with a fixed n and seeds, fixed
    95	  before results, and a task-level analysis (per-task mean over samples, sign test on per-task differences).
    96	  - ON-ADOPT: on-only > off-only, p < 0.2, AND ON timeouts <= OFF timeouts + 2, AND the cap-3.5 timing check passes.
    97	  - ON-BETTER-VETOED: on-only > off-only with p < 0.2 but the timeout or timing condition fails: keep OFF for shipping; report
    98	    to the Director with the timing data as a candidate for a cap/budget follow-up (no automatic further arm).
    99	  - KEEP-OFF: off-only >= on-only.
   100	  - NO-DIFFERENCE: on ahead with p >= 0.2: keep OFF (cheaper, faster). +-3 tasks on 33 is noise.
   101	  - Cap-3.5 timing check (cap unchanged, so this checks that thinking does not break cap enforcement): every ON row has a non-null
   102	    agent_clock_seconds <= 3.5 x 60 + 10 = 220 s and finalization_seconds <= 30 s; any violation or null fails the check.
   103	- Cost note: verification adds a fresh sandbox setup per task (Container B, two dependency installs), so per-task wall is higher than
   104	  the plan-005 screens (~5.5 min/task); the smoke measures it. If arm 2 at k=1 does not fit next week's quota with other approved work,
   105	  the arm-2 schedule comes back to the Director with the measured numbers.
