    41	
    42	### Row classification (frozen before any run; mechanical, from the raw timing.jsonl row)
    43	- KNOWN-DIAG (not an error): editable_failed=True where every failing editable subprocess output contains `uninstall-no-record-file`.
    44	  This is the documented scorer-harness RECORD strip (docs/GOLD_CALIBRATION.md v2, report 005-prelim): flat-layout rich/fastapi
    45	  import from /workspace via cwd, and the 48-clean gold/null calibration was done in the same docker-path where it occurs. It was
    46	  on 7/8 rows of every plan-005/006 kernel (results/kaggle_timing_31b_v00{1,3,5,6,7,8}.json). Counted and listed, never gating.
    47	- HARNESS error (H), exactly these: H-ROW = row missing, or the row's `error` field non-null (agent_timing.py sets it only for the
    48	  fail-closed harness_error, an evaluation/cleanup exception, or a trace-parse failure; normal agent end states such as
    49	  timeout/turns/tool_calls/no_submit leave it null); H-SETUP = setup_failed for any reason other than KNOWN-DIAG (a fatal setup step rc != 0,
    50	  missing_tool_deps, or an editable failure without `uninstall-no-record-file`); H-VERIFY = the row's filtered patch is non-empty
    51	  but exit_code is not an integer in 0..5 (verification never returned a pytest exit code). vLLM not up = the
    52	  whole kernel is void.
    53	- Everything else is an AGENT outcome and is a quality result, never a validity question: PASS = stock resolved=True;
    54	  FAIL sub-labels: no/empty patch (stock evaluate_task returns resolved=False, exit -1, verification not run, evaluate.py:324),
    55	  timeout, pytest exit 1, pytest exit 2-5 (e.g. the patch breaks collection), exit 0 but resolved=False (JUnit/required nodes).
    56	
    57	### Smoke, chunks, reruns
    58	- SMOKE first: the first 3 ids (eval/plans/007-smoke-ids.txt: 2 rich + 1 fastapi), budget 5400 s (rev 1: was 4800; fits the larger stop-guard reserve). The gate checks mechanics
    59	  only; agent quality (0/3 included) never fails it. Gate holds iff: vLLM up, 3 rows present, 0 H rows. On hold the smoke rows
    60	  COUNT as the first 3 arm-1 rows, and the main kernel runs ids 4..33 with --seed-max = ceil(max smoke per-task total).
    61	  Gate FAIL: no main run today; diagnose; the run moves after the reset (dec 062 item 4: no rushing).
    62	- Budget: KERNEL_BUDGET for main sized from the smoke per-task wall and the quota left before the reset (target: week
    63	  usage <= 29.5/30 h). Unrun ids (a suffix of the fixed order) run as chunk 2 after the reset, identical bundle and code SHA,
    64	  with --seed-max from all earlier rows.
    65	- First attempts are always retained and reported. A code change during arm 1 is allowed ONLY to fix a defect behind an H row,
    66	  documented first (journal line naming the row + the H category + the cause, then a commit, then a codex review). If the fix
    67	  touches no file on the agent or verification path, only the H rows rerun (appended at the end of the order). If it does
    68	  touch either path, every row already run reruns under the fixed code so all primary rows share one code SHA, and the
    69	  first-attempt rows are reported as a sensitivity line. Any bundle byte change = a different arm: arm 1 restarts with a new addendum.
    70	  No rerun for any AGENT outcome, ever.
    71	- Quota logged before/after every kernel in ops/budget/kaggle.md. No GCP spend. Never delays the dec 055 checklist at 2026-11-07T00:00Z.
